Hi @DeMoorJasper, so I was wondering the following, given that by default the html asset post process removes the text/css and the application/javascript type property of the tag as long as the `node.tag === "style"` or the type is application/javascript, do I remove that behaviour and rather insert the valid type property inside the script and style tag? or should I leave the behaviour as is, which removes the type property of style and js scripts?

See my previous fix does add application/javascript to the type prop of the script tag, however this lines in the HTML Asset post process remove those types:

```
        // Delete "type" attribute, since CSS and JS are the defaults.
        // Unless it's application/ld+json
        if (
          node.attrs &&
          (node.tag === 'style' ||
            (node.attrs.type && SCRIPT_TYPES[node.attrs.type] === 'js'))
        ) {
          delete node.attrs.type;
        }
``` 

That happens after inserting the correct type tag.

